  "term": "appetite suppressant",
  "definition": "An appetite suppressant is a substance or drug that reduces feeding behavior or food intake. In this packet, the term is used for anti-obesity drugs such as tesofensine and phentermine that lessen appetite and can contribute to weight loss.",
